                  <provenance type="#bc"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_601">Worcester,
                        Worcestershire. Benedictine cathedral priory of St Mary the Virgin.
                        </orgName><p>Binding leaves from the same motet book as leaves in Bodleian,
                        Lat. liturg. d. 20 (from the bindings of Auct. F. inf. 1. 3 and Bodley 862),
                        and in Worcester Add. 68 (nos 10, 11 and 28 from the bindings of F.125,
                        F.133 and F.34). The name 'musard' appears on fol. 5 (s. xv): cf. 'Johannes
                        musard' in Worcester F.90 and F.93. In addition, fol. 9 contains a copy of a
                        letter from Stephen, archbishop of Arles addressed to the monks of Worcester
                        and all the religious of the diocese. At 27 December, the Calendar has
                        'Obiit Robertus Dymhok pater Ade de Cyrencestria' (s.
                     xiii2).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Tenison sale, Sotheby's, 1 July 1861 (lot
                     86).</provenance>
